  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Ilopango-Aguacayo Hydropower, through Government of El Salvador</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $742,380 Ilopango-Aguacayo Hydropower Feasibility Study is supporting the development of a 17 megawatt (MW) hydropower facility on Lake Ilopango in El Salvador. The project would provide a reliable supply of renewable energy, while at the same time helping to control periodic flooding of the lake&apos;s surrounding areas. The Ilopango - Aguacayo Hydropower Project is a high priority project that would support the Obama Administration&apos;s Energy and Climate Partnership of the Americas and the Partnership for Growth initiative with El Salvador.</narrative>
  </description>
